  "slug": "design-novo-e389",
  "summary": "Recent RNA foundation models and ribosome-profiling-trained generative designers extend sequence modeling from prediction toward translational design.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is sequence-level modeling applied to nucleic acids for design rather than prediction alone. RiboDecode, a deep generative framework trained on ribosome profiling data, designs mRNA codon sequences that enhance translation and therapeutic efficacy. HydraRNA is a full-length RNA foundation model combining bidirectional state space and multi-head attention, pretrained on mRNAs and ncRNAs. MOSAIC applies Monte Carlo simulated annealing to harmonize linked codons toward native translation speed in heterologous expression, tested on ribosomal protein genes. A transformer encoder with Monte Carlo dropout designs convergent overlapping genes across three reading frames. SignalGen (signal peptide design) and IonNTXpred (ion channel modulator prediction) share the sequence-model framing without nucleic acid input. What is new is the shift from prediction toward sequence design judged by functional or translational readouts.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2025-11-16"
}
